=== Which of these can a recursive-descent parser handle? ===
  Left-recursive arithmetic          LEFT-RECURSIVE: ['E', 'T']
  Right-recursive arithmetic         no direct left recursion
  Balanced parentheses               no direct left recursion

=== The two arithmetic grammars generate the SAME strings ===
  left-recursive  E -> E + T | T      generates T, T+T, T+T+T, ...
  right-recursive E -> T E'           generates T, T+T, T+T+T, ...
  with E' -> + T E' | epsilon
  Same language. Different tree shape, and different parser fate.

=== Watch the trap, without actually hanging ===
  parse_E called itself 12 times, consuming nothing
  No input was consumed, so the base case is never reachable.
